                <head>219. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>NSC 5520, “U.S. Scientific Satellite Program,” was discussed by the National
                    Security Council at its May 26, 1955, meeting and approved by the President on
                    May 27. The potential for intelligence collection was a major factor in the
                    decision to proceed with satellite development. NSC 5520 is printed in <ref
                        target="frus:frus1955-57v11/pg_723"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1955–1957, volume XI, pages 723</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus:frus1955-57v11/pg_732">732</ref>.</p>
            </div>
